(4) The following types of study deferment will not be counted as utilized
semesters, in addition to Section 3, Article 7(2):
(a) students deferred by the University due to GPA < 1.00 in the previous
semester;
(b) students deferred by the University due to disciplinary action;

(c) students deferred for national interest, with a maximum period of two (2)
years or four (4) semesters. For each deferment application, the University
will approve two (2) semesters period, and students may apply to extend
the deferment as needed, subject to a maximum of four (4) semesters;
(d) students deferred due to participation in a Gap Y ear program;
(e) students deferred due to there are no courses offered in the given semester;

